  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only model (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer, config_006) achieves 0.653 acc, while the only multimodal experiment (config_030: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat) achieves only 0.632 acc—worse than RNA-only. Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23 acc). This suggests either the image features are pure noise or the concat fusion is diluting the strong RNA signal. Question tested: config_031 changes only the fusion strategy (concat → weighted) relative to config_030, isolating whether a weighted combination can preserve the RNA signal while leveraging any residual image information. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison that directly answers whether multimodal fusion is viable with the current image encoder. If weighted fusion recovers performance to ~0.65+, it validates pursuing multimodal with better encoders; if it remains below RNA-only, it strongly indicates resnet50 image features are not contributing useful signal, redirecting budget toward either a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) or consolidating effort on the RNA-only pipeline."
